---
.title = "Build Dynamic Output with Io.Writer.Allocating",
.date = "2024-01-01",
.author = "ZigCC",
.layout = "section.shtml",
---

Use `std.Io.Writer.Allocating` when the final output size is not known in advance. It owns a
growable buffer, exposes the completed bytes through `written()`, and releases its allocation with
`deinit()`.

